   "max_blocks": 1,
   "why_triggers": "Implementer choice: whether error handling is outside the requirements needs the user's request, which Semgrep cannot read. So the rule never refuses a write and does not scan the project at the end of the turn (which would repeat the same finding every turn): after a write or an edit it tells the agent once (max_blocks 1 per turn and trigger), and the agent decides. Files written by shell commands are not checked for this rule.",
